00:31:27,580 --> 00:31:29,460
开的还是一辆又小又便宜的
日本廉价两厢车。
in a small, cheap
Japanese hatchback.

532
00:31:29,500 --> 00:31:31,340
女士们先生们，
大卫·丁布尔比！
Ladies and gentlemen,
David Dimbleby!

533
00:31:31,380 --> 00:31:32,820
[观众欢呼]
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

534
00:31:35,260 --> 00:31:36,060
[模糊不清的问候声]
[GREETING INDISTINCTLY]

535
00:31:38,380 --> 00:31:39,980
请坐。
Have a seat.

536
00:31:40,020 --> 00:31:40,860
谢谢。
Thank you.

537
00:31:43,180 --> 00:31:44,420
谢谢。
Thank you.

538
00:31:44,460 --> 00:31:47,220
泰斗亲临啊，
The master himself,

539
00:31:47,260 --> 00:31:48,860
一代宗师来到了我们中间。
the master is among us.

540
00:31:48,900 --> 00:31:52,020
你们家可真算得上是
播音主持界的豪门望族，对吧？
You really are a part of
a broadcasting
dynasty, aren't you?

541
00:31:52,060 --> 00:31:55,900
呃，家里确实还有别人
干播音主持这行，是的。
Um, there have been
other people in my family
who've been broadcasters, yes.

542
00:31:55,940 --> 00:31:57,460
你兄弟在独立电视台（ITV），还有令尊，
Your brother on ITV,
and your father,

543
00:31:57,500 --> 00:31:59,860
BBC 广播电台新闻节目基本就是他开创的，对吧？
he pretty much started
BBC Radio news, didn't he?

544
00:31:59,900 --> 00:32:02,180
BBC 广播电台新闻确实是他开创的。
He did start BBC Radio news.

545
00:32:02,220 --> 00:32:04,060
那你的孩子们
也打算入这行吗？
So, are your kids
going into broadcasting?

546
00:32:04,100 --> 00:32:08,060
因为等他们进电视圈的时候，
电视上播的恐怕就只剩下……
Because by the time
they get into TV,
it's just going to be...

547
00:32:08,100 --> 00:32:10,380
-《全英最沉铺路石板》。
-没错。
-Britain's Heaviest
Paving Slab.
-Yes.

548
00:32:10,420 --> 00:32:13,140
还有《全英最脏高尔夫球》，
全都是一堆垃圾烂节目。
and Britain's Muddiest
Golfball,and it'll all
just be rubbish.

549
00:32:13,180 --> 00:32:15,340
-不，绝不至于沦落成那样。
-你觉得不会？
-No, it will
never be like that.
-You don't think so?

550
00:32:15,380 --> 00:32:17,420
我们刚拍完《英国画卷》，
反响简直……
We've been doing this
A Picture of Britainthing,
and it's had a fan...

551
00:32:17,460 --> 00:32:19,820
我干了45年电视，
I've been in television
45 years,

552
00:32:19,860 --> 00:32:23,060
我还从来没……你永远不知道
一个节目到底能不能火，
I've never had...
You never know whether
a thing's gonna work or not,

553
00:32:23,100 --> 00:32:25,300
而这部片子竟然瞬间引爆全场。
And this has suddenly
hit the bull's eye.

554
00:32:25,340 --> 00:32:29,260
所以说……这说明大家其实
还是喜欢严肃节目的。
So things... It means people
like serious programming.

555
00:32:29,300 --> 00:32:30,900
不过依我看，那节目
Which, as far as
I can work out,

556
00:32:30,940 --> 00:32:33,740
主要就是开车晃悠在
mostly involves driving down

557
00:32:33,780 --> 00:32:38,020
风景绝美、连辆鬼影子都没有的公路上。
也太脱离现实了吧！
really beautiful, empty roads.
Bit unrealistic!

558
00:32:38,060 --> 00:32:40,420
恕我冒昧……我真不知道
你哪来这种印象！
If I may be so... I don't know
where you got that idea from!

559
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:45,260
可我们走的是抒情路线，你懂吧，
我们希望呈现出
But we were doing lyrical,
you see, we wanted it to look

560
00:32:45,300 --> 00:32:48,260
宁静祥和、抚慰人心的感觉。
calming and reassuring.

561
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:52,900
我选这辆车的理由
就是它特别不起眼，
那辆路虎。
The reason I chose this car
was it was just unobtrusive,
the Land Rover.

562
00:32:52,940 --> 00:32:54,580
其实我们今天把它弄来了。
We've got it here, actually.

563
00:32:54,620 --> 00:32:56,700
丁布尔比：它居然没散架一路开过来，
我真是惊呆了！
DIMBLEBY:I'm amazed
it arrived in one piece!

564
00:32:56,740 --> 00:32:58,140
克拉克森：今天早上我还看了看你那辆车。
CLARKSON: I was looking at
your one this morning.

565
00:32:58,180 --> 00:33:00,180
只要瞧瞧上面的机械工程设计，
简直能笑死人。
It is hysterical when you look
at the engineering on it.

566
00:33:00,220 --> 00:33:03,100
“哎，这后尾门需要几个铰链。
"Well, we need some hinges
for this back door.

567
00:33:03,140 --> 00:33:05,780
我家花园铁门上有几个，
反正是铰链，凑合用吧。”
"There's some from
my garden gate,
they're hinges, they'll do."

568
00:33:05,820 --> 00:33:10,060
-上面的每一个零部件……
-传动轴在高速公路上掉下来了，
-Every single bit of it...
-The drive shaft
fell off on the motorway,

569
00:33:10,100 --> 00:33:13,180
前轮在高速公路上爆胎了，
the front tyre blew
on the motorway,

570
00:33:13,220 --> 00:33:15,900
还有那个……呃，
叫什么刹车来着？
the, um, what do you
call that, brake?

571
00:33:15,940 --> 00:33:17,540
-手刹。
-……手刹断了。
-Handbrake.
-.Handbrake broke.

572
00:33:17,580 --> 00:33:21,020
-完全不灵。
-你随时可以挂挡别住嘛。
-Didn't work at all.
-You can always
put it in gear.

573
00:33:21,060 --> 00:33:23,340
而且美妙之处在于，
当你开着这车到处跑，
And the nice thing is,
when you're driving
around in the car,

574
00:33:23,380 --> 00:33:24,900
我们在冬天开得特别多，
we did a lot of it
in the winter,

575
00:33:24,940 --> 00:33:27,060
外面下雨车里漏雨，外面下雪车里飘雪，
the rain comes in,
and the snow comes in,

576
00:33:27,100 --> 00:33:29,940
你坐里面甚至感觉自己
完全置身在大自然中。
and you're sitting there
and you feel you're
out in the open air.

577
00:33:29,980 --> 00:33:31,620
这么说，你是那种觉得
So, are you one of
these people that
thinks that

578
00:33:31,660 --> 00:33:35,540
公路多多少少破坏了乡村风光的人吗？
roads have somehow
spoiled the countryside?

579
00:33:35,580 --> 00:33:39,140
这个真不好说。
不过我觉得在一点上确实破坏了，
I don't know, really.
I mean, I'll tell you
one way they've spoilt it,

580
00:33:39,180 --> 00:33:41,100
那就是，如果你去……
which is, if you go...

581
00:33:41,140 --> 00:33:45,940
我们去了两百年前
那些大画家去过的地方。
We went to places where
painters had been,
you know, 200 years ago.

582
00:33:45,980 --> 00:33:49,660
那里的景色和两百年前一模一样，
And the scene would be exactly
as it was 200 years ago,

583
00:33:49,700 --> 00:33:52,620
但耳边却总有这种嗡嗡的噪音，
而且是……
but there would be
this hum all the time
and it would be...

584
00:33:52,660 --> 00:33:56,340
其实那是在肯特郡，
是去多佛的高速公路传来的。
This was in Kent, in fact,
and it was the
motorway to Dover.

585
00:33:56,380 --> 00:33:59,860
双向四车道就是会一直发出这种持续不断的噪音。
Dual carriageways make
just this constant noise.

586
00:33:59,900 --> 00:34:01,980
但公路其实很美啊。看着高速公路蜿蜒延展……
But they are beautiful.
To watch a motorway snaking...

587
00:34:02,020 --> 00:34:04,500
比如M6高速，
蜿蜒穿过……如果是航拍镜头的话，
The M6,
when it snakes through,
if you get an aerial shot,

588
00:34:04,540 --> 00:34:06,620
蜿蜒穿过湖区，
snakes through
the Lake District,

589
00:34:06,660 --> 00:34:10,660
那真是最壮观的……
高速公路本身就是不可思议的工程杰作。
that is one of the most...
They're wonderful pieces
of engineering, motorways.

590
00:34:10,700 --> 00:34:12,540
曾经有人这么跟我形容M1高速。
Somebody once described
the M1 to me.

591
00:34:12,580 --> 00:34:16,820
他说：“你就把它想象成一座高两百英里的摩天大楼，
He said, "Imagine it
as a skyscraper,
200 miles tall,

592
00:34:16,860 --> 00:34:19,740
只是放倒在地上而已。”
它的复杂程度就是如此惊人。
"but lying on its side."
That's how complicated
they are.

593
00:34:19,780 --> 00:34:21,060
反正我每次看着它们都会想：
I mean, I just
look at them
and think,

594
00:34:21,100 --> 00:34:22,780
“比两边的任何风景都好看多了。”
"Much better than anything
on either side."

595
00:34:22,820 --> 00:34:25,260
但你总不至于……【笑】
But you don't... [LAUGHS]

596
00:34:25,300 --> 00:34:29,300
所以你难不成想把野餐桌
摆在高速公路正中间？
So you'd like to set up
your picnic table
in the middle of the motorway?

597
00:34:29,340 --> 00:34:31,340
稍微往路边靠一点就行。
Slightly off to one side.

598
00:34:31,380 --> 00:34:34,900
为什么大家到了目的地之后
都不下车呢？
Why don't people
get out of their cars
when they do reach a place?

599
00:34:34,940 --> 00:34:36,780
这点我实在是搞不懂。
'Cause that's
disconcerting to me.

600
00:34:36,820 --> 00:34:38,900
据统计好像是
I think the statistic is

601
00:34:38,940 --> 00:34:43,460
他们离开车子的距离，
平均下来，
居然不会超过两百码。
that they don't move
more than 200 yards,
on average, from the car.

602
00:34:43,500 --> 00:34:44,780
还能走那么远？
That far?

603
00:34:46,740 --> 00:34:48,620
言归正传，说回
《不列颠掠影》，
Anyway, going back to
Picture of Britain,

604
00:34:48,660 --> 00:34:50,540
据我所知，你收到了
不少观众投诉，
you've had, I understand,
a number of complaints

605
00:34:50,580 --> 00:34:53,220
都是针对你开那辆
路虎时的驾驶风格。
about the way you drove
your Land Rover.

606
00:34:53,260 --> 00:34:54,980
没错，一点不假。
Yeah, absolutely.

607
00:34:55,020 --> 00:34:59,420
都是因为边开边聊。你知道的，
我一说话就喜欢手舞足蹈。
Because of talking. You see,
I use my hands when I talk.

608
00:34:59,460 --> 00:35:03,980
摄像师就坐在你旁边，
就像你现在坐的位置一样。
And the cameraman's
sitting beside you,
like where you are.

609
00:35:04,020 --> 00:35:07,580
我一边开车一边讲：
“关于什罗普郡这个地方啊……哎呀！”
Driving along,
"The thing about Shropshire
is... Whoops!"

610
00:35:07,620 --> 00:35:09,220
一边换挡，
一边继续滔滔不绝。
Changing gear and
going on talking.

611
00:35:09,260 --> 00:35:11,020
你对行车安全不是很上心，
对吧？
You're not big on safety,
are you?

612
00:35:11,060 --> 00:35:14,060
我向来不吃那一套
所谓的“安全法西斯主义”。
I don't believe
in what I call safety fascism.

613
00:35:14,100 --> 00:35:15,820
我们家以前有辆车，
刚把它给处理掉，
We had a car,
we've just got
rid of it,

614
00:35:15,860 --> 00:35:17,620
我想那车还是你的心头好之一呢，
which I think is one
of your favourites,

615
00:35:17,660 --> 00:35:19,180
是一辆沃尔沃……
which is a Volvo...

616
00:35:19,220 --> 00:35:20,860
-那辆大号的……
-XC90。
-The big...
-The XC90.

617
00:35:20,900 --> 00:35:24,940
开起来又软又晃荡，
而且一点提速都没有，
It was so soft and rolly
and no acceleration,

618
00:35:24,980 --> 00:35:27,020
但最让我们火大的是，
but the thing
that really irritated us,

619
00:35:27,060 --> 00:35:31,300
只要你没系安全带，
它就会把收音机声音调小，
if you didn't put
your seatbelt on,
it turned the radio down

620
00:35:31,340 --> 00:35:34,220
直到你把安全带系上为止！
你能信吗？
until you put
your seatbelt on!
Can you believe that?

621
00:35:34,260 --> 00:35:36,060
你正听着新闻呢，
You're listening to the news,

622
00:35:36,100 --> 00:35:38,820
“各位听众好，
现在由某某为您播报新闻。”
"Here is the news
with so-and-so."

623
00:35:38,860 --> 00:35:40,540
“首相刚刚宣布……”
"The Prime Minister
has announced..."

624
00:35:40,580 --> 00:35:43,060
[含糊不清的嘟囔声]
[MUMBLES INAUDIBLY]

625
00:35:43,100 --> 00:35:44,740
怎么没声了？
赶紧把安全带系上！
What's happened?
Put your seatbelt on.

626
00:35:44,780 --> 00:35:47,140
-要是维京人当年……
-就是。
-How far would the
Vikings have got...
-Yes.

627
00:35:47,180 --> 00:35:50,380
……在长船上都得系安全带，
他们能打下多大疆土？
...if they had to put
their seatbelts on
in their longboats?

628
00:35:50,420 --> 00:35:53,060
“弟兄们，我们要去抢劫掠夺啦！
拿斧子小心点别伤着自己。”
"We're going raping
and pillaging.
And careful with that axe."

629
00:35:53,100 --> 00:35:55,940
它凭什么在老子自己的车里指手画脚？
How dare they tell me
what to do in my car?

630
00:35:55,980 --> 00:36:00,820
得了吧，你这纯属胡搅蛮缠了，
虽说你向来如此，但你这……
No, you're being foolish now,
which is not unknown,
but you are...

631
00:36:00,860 --> 00:36:03,300
-你这也太不可理喻了……
-我这是夸张修辞手法！
-You're being very foolish...
-I'm using hyperbole.

632
00:36:03,340 --> 00:36:04,820
噢！合着你是在秀聪明是吧？
Oh! You're being clever, then?

633
00:36:04,860 --> 00:36:07,700
没错！你看，
这两者区别可大了去了。
Yes! See,
there's a big difference.

634
00:36:07,740 --> 00:36:09,020
我能聊聊你的买车历史吗？
Can I talk about
your car history?

635
00:36:09,060 --> 00:36:10,500
因为我们请过很多人来上节目，
Because we have
a number of people come on,

636
00:36:10,540 --> 00:36:12,460
他们开过的车大多无聊透顶。
and mostly they've had
very boring cars.

637
00:36:12,500 --> 00:36:15,900
坦白讲，你的车史是所有人里
最精彩、最有意思的。
You have the best,
most interesting car history,
frankly, of anybody.

638
00:36:15,940 --> 00:36:19,340
因为你开过
蓝旗亚Fulvia、
NSU RO80、
Because you had
a Lancia Fulvia,
an NSU RO80,

639
00:36:19,380 --> 00:36:22,600
-一辆简森Interceptor和一辆布里斯托。
-还有一辆阳光Alpine。
-a Jensen Interceptor
and a Bristol.
-And a Sunbeam Alpine.

640
00:36:22,620 --> 00:36:25,820
居然还有辆Alpine？
这车单简直太绝了。
And an Alpine as well?
That's a great collection of cars.

641
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:27,540
确实相当棒。
- 我们这儿有张Ro80的照片
Yeah, they were really good.
- We've got a picture of the Ro80 here

642
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:29,260
专门给那些年纪太轻、
根本没见过它的人开开眼。
for those of you who were
too young to remember it.

643
00:36:29,280 --> 00:36:31,680
所有人年纪都太轻，没谁记得它。
- 哪有，我还记得呢。
Everybody's too young to remember it.
- No, I can remember it.

644
00:36:31,700 --> 00:36:34,500
那车当年真是太超前了。
- 这照片拍得可真够烂的！
That was so far ahead of its time.
- That's a terrible picture!

645
00:36:34,520 --> 00:36:41,120
没错，棕色的，1975年P字车牌。
不过Ro80可是出了名的
Yes it's brown, 1975 P-Reg.
The Ro80 though was notorious for its

646
00:36:41,140 --> 00:36:46,140
汪克尔转子发动机老是坏掉。
- 没错。我跟你讲件关于它的事。
Wankel rotary engine always going wrong.
- Yeah. I'll tell you a thing about it.

647
00:36:46,160 --> 00:36:51,260
那发动机是有质保的，气缸里转动的
那些碳质顶角，
The engine was guaranteed and the
carbon tips on the cylinder went round,

648
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:55,980
对吧，那些碳质顶端……
总是不停地磨损报废。
right, and there was a carbon tip...
always wore out.

649
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:58,400
对，早该用钻石做才对。
- 然后你开车在路上的时候，
Yeah. Should have been diamond.
- And when you were driving along,

650
00:36:58,420 --> 00:37:02,420
要是迎面擦肩开过另一辆，你俩就会伸出手指，
比划自己换过几台发动机了。
if you passed another one, you held up your
fingers for how many engines you'd had.

651
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:05,840
真的假的？
- 真的！“嗨！第四台了！”
Really?
- Yeah. Hello! Four!

652
00:37:05,860 --> 00:37:09,160
（絮絮叨叨）反正都在保修期内，
根本一分钱不用你掏。
(RAMBLING) They were under guarantee,
they never cost you anything.

653
00:37:09,180 --> 00:37:10,880
哦，厂家直接全免费？
- 后来他们干脆放弃了。
Oh, they just did it for free?
- And then they gave up.

654
00:37:10,900 --> 00:37:14,700
他们彻底放弃治疗，把最后一台塞进了
科学博物馆，到现在还在那儿呢。
They gave up and put the last one in the
Science Museum, where it's still today.

655
00:37:14,720 --> 00:37:17,120
那台Ro80还在那儿吗？
- 没，就那台发动机还在。
Is it still there, the Ro80?
- No, no, just the engine.

656
00:37:17,140 --> 00:37:17,720
就发动机，没错。
The engine, yep.

657
00:37:17,740 --> 00:37:21,860
有意思的来了。
我正在看你的
这份拥车名单，对吧？
This is what is interesting.
I'm looking at your
list of cars, okay?

658
00:37:21,900 --> 00:37:23,700
通常来说，买车总能找到共同点。
Normally there's a link.

659
00:37:23,740 --> 00:37:25,460
我回顾一下自己这些年来
拥有过的
